{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs7AKmdTg6WTkDzkiuV2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `name_key` in `contacts/dedupe.py`, and the reproduction test now passes (1 passed). I didn't change the test or add new tests. I checked the Mac/Windows and `ß` cases with a one-off script instead.\n\nThere were three root causes, all in `name_key`:\n\n1. **Accents:** only a hard-coded list of 8 accented letters was stripped, so any other accented letter (`ç`, `ô`, `ł`, `ø` and so on) stayed distinct. It now decomposes the name with NFKD and drops all combining marks.\n2. **Mac vs. Windows:** a decomposed name (`u` followed by a combining mark, as macOS produces) never matched the precomposed form (`ü`), because only the precomposed characters were in the list. NFKD handles both forms.\n3. **`ß` vs. `ss`:** `.lower()` leaves `ß` unchanged. It now uses `.casefold()`, which turns `ß` into `ss`.\n\nWhitespace handling is now applied after normalization. That also collapses non-breaking spaces, which are common in pasted names.\n\n`\"Straße Müller\"`, `\"STRASSE  Mu\\u0308ller\"` and `\"Strasse\\u00a0Muller\"` now produce the same key. The first-seen record is still the one kept.\n\nOne thing I left alone: a skipped duplicate's other key isn't recorded. If record B matches A by name and B has a second email, a later record C with that email won't be merged into A. I didn't change it because the right behavior there is a product decision. I can change it if you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4935,"cache_read_input_tokens":26785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4935},"output_tokens":519,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1